    "show_share": true,
    "description": "While the need for surgical care has been rapidly increasing in Pakistan, the capacity of the healthcare system has not expanded at the same pace to cater these needs. COVID-19 has widened the gap further with financial implications on healthcare system, education and research. That means, more people could die from treatable common surgical conditions, warned experts while speaking at the inaugural session of the 6th AKU Annual Surgical Conference, Surgical Education and Training: Developing Standards.",
